After playing a full game, Here is my prognosis. The gameplay has great potential, and looking back, theres been some real progress with this games vertical slice, we are almost there, just need the gameplay ironed out, and player movement that makes it FEEL like baseball. The replays need to be the "in-between"/ result of what happens. I've been saying I want a fluid baseball game, and that stems from the frustration I feel playing this currently. players scooring on groundout from second, fielders not having any sort of AI. Hey can an AI build an intriqete baseball CPU that WANTS to beat the player, but also produces fun moments for them. This project has been really fun working on, and I hope with the gameplay imporvements and my music, it can have potential to be real deal.
